      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sealy was named for George Sealy, a Gulf, Colorado and Santa Fe Railroad director, when the town was founded in 1879.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ci.sealy.tx.us/welcome/about_sealy/historical_facts/index.php",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1881 Daniel Haynes opened a cotton‑filled mattress factory that would later give the world the Sealy Mattress Company its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        20,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ci.sealy.tx.us/welcome/about_sealy/historical_facts/index.php",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Haynes expanded the mattress business in 1909, opening a new factory on a fresh site that helped cement Sealy’s reputation for innovation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ci.sealy.tx.us/welcome/about_sealy/historical_facts/index.php",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic Liedertafel, meaning “Song Hall,” was built as a gathering place for plays, concerts, and dancing in the early 1900s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
